# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Playwright browser cache. shoot.mjs drives chromium; the binaries land either
# in the user cache (ms-playwright) or, when PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=0, inside
# node_modules. Hundreds of megabytes either way — never committed.
.local-browsers/
ms-playwright/
.playwright/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Review renders. Seven art-director passes produced 1.9 GB of PNGs, and every
# one is regenerable: the build is deterministic and gated by tools/determinism.py,
# so `node tools/render/town.mjs` reproduces any frame exactly. The reports in
# review/reports/ ARE tracked — they are the argument, and they cite the frames.
review/shots/

# Generated assets (D-067). Every file under assets/ is deterministic output of
# tools/assetgen: a fresh clone runs `make setup && make assets` and gets
# byte-identical meshes and textures. Git was carrying 410 MB of regenerable
# binaries, and townhouse.bin (63 MB) had crossed GitHub's 50 MB warning line.
# Git keeps the source of truth (generators, content/, docs); the generated
# state is covered by timestamped zips in backups/ (SessionStart hook ->
# tools/backup.ps1), which OneDrive carries off-machine.
assets/
backups/

# Local Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
